\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {VIII}{\ignorespaces Tail metrics with cluster-bootstrap 95\% intervals over synthesis replicates (baseline). Extreme quantiles estimated from a few hundred retrievals are imprecise, and the intervals of most policies overlap; the ordering of the means does not carry over to q99. $\Delta $q99: paired difference in q99 against round-robin on the same syntheses and read orders, in reads, with its cluster-bootstrap 95\% interval; this is the interval quoted in the text. Thousands of reads unless stated.}}{16}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:r4tails}{{VIII}{16}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {IX}{\ignorespaces Secondary evidence: semi-empirical replay of real Illumina read streams (ENA PRJEB65931), generic prior, no evaluation-split statistics. Mean reads (thousands) and q99; $\Delta $: mean minus the hindsight-tuned static budget (paired bootstrap 95\% CI). Decodability is an oracle event here (consensus equals the designed strand), so this is \emph  {not} exact retrieval.}}{16}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:replay}{{IX}{16}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {\mbox  {VI-F}}Secondary evidence: real read streams}{16}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:res-replay}{{\mbox  {VI-F}}{16}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {X}{\ignorespaces What the calibrated prior costs (Genscript replay, coverage-greedy). Calibration reads are charged explicitly: they are the first reads of the same six sequencing runs, disjoint from the evaluation reads. Break-even is the number of retrievals over which the calibration reads are repaid by the per-retrieval saving against round-robin. Thousands of reads.}}{17}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:r4calcost}{{X}{17}{}{}{}}
